	// Magic effects used by recipes. "form" pins each key to a vanilla magic effect; vanilla
	// FormIDs are the same in every language and edition, and overhauls that change an
	// effect edit that record, so their version is used. The SKSE log lists every alchemy
	// magic effect in your load order in this format, for add-ons that use other effects.
	// If a form is missing, the key is matched by actor value, archetype and flags instead,
	// picking the effect used most often by ingredients and potions.
	// "nameContains" / "nameExcludes" (a word or a list) narrow that fallback by the English
	// effect name, where properties alone can't tell effects apart (Damage, Lingering Damage
	// and Ravage). They are never consulted when the form resolves.
	// "duration" replaces the vanilla base duration (seconds) that tiers, quality and traits
	// scale from. The gold value still uses the vanilla duration.
	// "base": {"magnitude", "duration"} are the values an ingredient would carry, for effects
	// no ingredient or potion in the game has; skill, perks and tiers scale them as usual.
	// "magnitudeScale" converts the magnitude shown in the menu into the game's (0.01 for an
	// actor value counted in fractions), "maxMagnitude" caps it (menu units), "maxDuration"
	// caps the duration (seconds).
